title: AudioCodes: LEDs
agents: snmp
catalog: agentless
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the state and color of AudioCodes LEDs.
 It evaluates all LEDs of the modules, fan trays and power supplies.
 The check ignores LEDs without a color and gray LEDs.

 The color of an LED sets the state: green is OK,
 yellow, orange and blue are WARN, red is CRIT.
 An LED with an undefined color is UNKN.
 On a MediaPack MP-124, a flashing red LED is OK.
 According to the MP-124 documentation, only the Data LED flashes red.
 It shows that the device receives RTP packets.

 On a MediaPack MP-124, the check ignores the LEDs of the channels above
 the number of ports that the device reports.
 If SRTP is enabled, the MP-124 can show these LEDs red.

 If the device does not report the name of a module, the check shows the module type.

discovery:
 One service is created.
